      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Update: after doing some testing, doing networking on Start for objects set active post scene load works perfectly fine.  This appears to be exclusively an issue with objects active on scene load.\n\nAlso in my testing, while RequestSerialization() failed to work on Start() for these objects, attempting it again a frame later did work.  The logs also might lend a clue as to what is happening (note, the \"Performing Serialization a second time\" log is made during Start(), before a SendCustomEventDelayedFrames is called)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
